{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016455-sorcerer-necromancy-paths","id":1016455,"title":"Sorcerer - Necromancy Paths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-13T01:25:20-08:00","id":1016455,"title":"Sorcerer - Necromancy Paths","content":"I was skimming through the Euthanatos Revised Trad Book, and read a short sidebar about Sorcerers within their ranks. It gave a short list of common Paths such characters can take (Divination, Fortune, Summoning/Binding/Warding), which were all well and good. Entirely appropriate. But it also advised Storytellers to create or modify Paths to handle other powers.<br /> <br /> This got me thinking about how, other than communing with ghosts and the like, not a lot of the common powers associated with Necromancy are covered by the Sorcerer or Sorcerer Revised rules. I do know that one of the Vampire books advises using their Paths for mortals, but they weren't built for mortal sorcerers in mind (and are fairly wonky to boot; the Bone Path abandons control of corpses halfway through to go into tearing souls out of the living and putting other souls in).<br /> <br /> Do or would any of you use existing Vampire material for unAwakened Necromancy? Or do you create your own original material? And if the latter, how do/would you construct Paths related to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T04:24:47-08:00","id":1016489,"title":"","content":"I sometimes used the mechanics from the merit \u201cStatic Shaman\u201c (Spirit Ways I think).<br /> Then just add fitting themes/descriptions to other mechanics (Path of Hellfire can be described via Necrosynthesis).<br /> <br /> And more often than not I don't concern me too much with rules and mechanics and sort of go with the flow of the story. Making powers up on the way.<br /> <br /> I have also done minimalist writeups of NPCs along the line of Offense Magic 7 dice, Defense 5, Restorative 0, Other 3.<br /> Over this structure I donned a blanket of PracticeResonanceSkinSortOf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T07:16:09-08:00","id":1016537,"title":"","content":"Or you could use VtM Necromancy. I believe that one of the new books has rules on mortals learning Necromancy. I would just let mortals learn Necromancy as Hedge Magic, allow them to use Willpower instead of Blood Pool, and increase the required time to perform Necromancy to ten turns per level of effect (or one hour per level for Rituals). The same could propably be done to transform any Blood Sorcery into Hedge Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:27:52-08:00","id":1016599,"title":"","content":"That does seem like it would work. The Necromancy discipline, at least as originally conceived, was supposed to be largely based on the work the Giovanni did as mortal necromancers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:14:36-08:00","id":1016623,"title":"","content":"Might also want to check out the Mediums book for Wraith.<br /> <br /> I would suggest Mana Manipulation to start with, and require Mana for the Necromancy Path rather than Blood Pool or Willpower. (And gaining the Mana requiring some rather icky spells and rituals. Possibly draining life from others or the caster.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T20:31:46-08:00","id":1016887,"title":"","content":"There are also some Paths in the Revised Dreamspeakers Tradition Book that could be adapted for use a necromancer. In particular, there's one that lets you manipulate Gauntlet. With minimal reskinning, I could see something like it but dealing with the Shroud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}